# IBM Code Engine BUILD-FROM-GIT deployment configuration for an MCP server.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in, then: `source ibm/code-engine-git-build/.env`
# before running the scripts.
#
# This file contains NO secrets — only non-sensitive deployment coordinates.
# Your IBM Cloud API key is NEVER stored here (see IBMCLOUD_API_KEY note below).
#
# What this kit does (vs. the sibling prebuilt-image kit):
#   Code Engine clones GIT_REPO_URL, builds its Dockerfile SERVER-SIDE, pushes
#   the resulting image to YOUR IBM Container Registry (ICR) namespace, then
#   deploys it. No local Docker, no local image build/push. This is the intended
#   "point Code Engine at your repo and go" flow — it requires ICR authority
#   (namespace create/write + a registry access secret) that the original trial
#   account lacked.

# --- IBM Cloud target ---------------------------------------------------------
# Region for the Code Engine project. Common: us-south, us-east, eu-de, eu-gb.
IBMCLOUD_REGION=us-east

# Resource group the project lives in. ALWAYS confirm with
# `ibmcloud resource groups` — many accounts have NO "Default" group. TechZone /
# trial accounts (e.g. itz-saas-*) typically expose a single generated group like
# `eid-<hash>`; use that exact name. A wrong value fails at `ibmcloud target -g`.
IBMCLOUD_RESOURCE_GROUP=Default

# --- Code Engine app ----------------------------------------------------------
# Code Engine project name (created if it does not exist).
CE_PROJECT=mcp-hackathon

# Name of the Code Engine application.
CE_APP_NAME=cdc-places-mcp-server

# Port the container listens on. This server's Dockerfile sets PORT=8080 and
# serves MCP (streamable-HTTP) at /mcp with a health check at /health.
CE_PORT=8080

# --- Git source (build-from-Git) ---------------------------------------------
# Public repo Code Engine will clone and build. Public repos only (hackathon
# scope is public data). A private repo would additionally need a Code Engine
# Git secret + --build-git-repo-secret; out of scope here.
#
# Example (this repo):
#   GIT_REPO_URL=https://github.com/GSA-TTS/cdc-places-mcp-server
#   GIT_BRANCH=feat/ibm-code-engine-deploy
GIT_REPO_URL=
GIT_BRANCH=main

# Subdirectory within the repo that contains the Dockerfile (build context).
# "." means the repo root. Change if your server lives in a subfolder.
GIT_CONTEXT_DIR=.

# Path to the Dockerfile, relative to GIT_CONTEXT_DIR.
GIT_DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile

# --- IBM Container Registry (build output target) ----------------------------
# ICR_REGION selects the registry the built image is pushed to; ICR_DOMAIN is the
# matching hostname. Confirm your account's registries with `ibmcloud cr region`
# (shows the currently targeted one) — NOT `ibmcloud cr regions`, which does not
# exist in current CLI versions.
#
#   global   -> icr.io      (default in many TechZone / itz-saas-* accounts)
#   us-south -> us.icr.io
#   eu-de    -> de.icr.io
#   eu-gb    -> uk.icr.io
#
# NOTE: the ICR region is independent of IBMCLOUD_REGION. A Code Engine app in
# us-east can push to the GLOBAL registry (icr.io) — that is a valid, common
# pairing. Set ICR_REGION/ICR_DOMAIN to whatever `ibmcloud cr region` reports.
ICR_REGION=global
ICR_DOMAIN=icr.io

# Namespace within ICR to push the built image into. The deploy script creates
# it if missing (create-or-reuse), but namespace-CREATE requires authority some
# trial accounts withhold. FIRST run `ibmcloud cr namespace-list`: if a shared
# namespace was pre-provisioned for you (e.g. `gsa-hackathon-cr-erm1`), set this
# to that name and reuse it — no create authority needed.
ICR_NAMESPACE=mcp-hackathon

# Tag applied to the built image. The full pushed image reference is:
#   ${ICR_DOMAIN}/${ICR_NAMESPACE}/${CE_APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG}
IMAGE_TAG=latest

# Name of the Code Engine registry-access secret the script creates/uses so CE
# can push the built image to ICR. This is a CE object name, not a credential.
CE_REGISTRY_SECRET=icr-push-secret

# --- IBM Cloud API key (NOT stored in this file) -----------------------------
# The registry-access secret is created from an IBM Cloud IAM API key. Provide
# it at runtime via the IBMCLOUD_API_KEY environment variable (NOT committed):
#
#   export IBMCLOUD_API_KEY="$(ibmcloud iam api-key-create ce-icr-push \
#       -d 'Code Engine ICR push' --output json | jq -r .apikey)"
#
# If IBMCLOUD_API_KEY is unset, the deploy script prompts for it (input hidden)
# and never writes it to disk. Rotate/delete the key when finished:
#   ibmcloud iam api-key-delete ce-icr-push
# IBMCLOUD_API_KEY=   # <- leave commented; set via `export` in your shell only
